quran[15]{c,v,t}:
  15,1,"Alif, Lam, Ra. These are the Verses of the Book and a Manifest Qur’an."
  15,2,The disbelievers will often wish (in the Hereafter) that they had been Muslims.
  15,3,"Leave them to eat and enjoy themselves, and let false hope distract them, for soon they will know."
  15,4,"We have never destroyed any town, but it had a known decree."
  15,5,"No nation can bring their time forward, nor can they delay it."
  15,6,And they say: ‘O you to whom the Reminder has been revealed! You are indeed insane.
  15,7,Why do you not bring us the angels if you are truthful?’
  15,8,"(Tell them:) We do not send down the angels, but with (the command of execution of) the judgement. And then they will not be granted any respite."
  15,9,"Indeed, We have revealed the Reminder, and surely, We are its Protectors."
  15,10,We indeed sent (messengers) before you to former communities.
  15,11,"And never did a messenger come to them, but they ridiculed him."
  15,12,That is how We pave the way for mockery and disbelief to enter the hearts of the guilty.
  15,13,"They do not believe in this (Qur’an), although the precedent of the ancients (destroyed before them) has already passed."
  15,14,"If We were to open a gateway to heaven for them so that they could continually ascend through it,"
  15,15,"they would (still) say: ‘Indeed, our eyes are hallucinated; rather, we are a bewitched people!’"
